WEBVTT

00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:01.142
Previously.

00:00:01.142 --> 00:00:04.670
On Sidefighter: The Week That Changed Everything.

00:00:05.820 --> 00:00:07.120
Six fighters.

00:00:07.120 --> 00:00:08.420
One fireball.

00:00:08.420 --> 00:00:09.520
No regrets.

00:00:09.520 --> 00:00:12.420
And one review, from one man.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:15.450
Kinda janky, he said.

00:00:15.450 --> 00:00:17.690
Basically, Mortal Kombat it.

00:00:20.040 --> 00:00:21.198
That man was Tony.

00:00:21.198 --> 00:00:22.999
This film is not about Tony.

00:00:22.999 --> 00:00:25.122
Tony would want you to know that.

00:00:25.122 --> 00:00:28.210
Tony would also want you to know about the jank.

00:00:30.360 --> 00:00:31.182
In the beginning...

00:00:31.182 --> 00:00:31.960
there was nothing.

00:00:34.510 --> 00:00:35.928
No sprites.

00:00:35.928 --> 00:00:36.959
No maps.

00:00:36.959 --> 00:00:37.990
No game.

00:00:40.340 --> 00:00:45.269
Just twelve thousand, one hundred and two three-dimensional models.

00:00:45.269 --> 00:00:45.931
Sleeping.

00:00:45.931 --> 00:00:46.740
In folders.

00:00:48.290 --> 00:00:50.379
Soldiers who had never walked.

00:00:50.379 --> 00:00:52.747
Tanks that had never fired a shot.

00:00:52.747 --> 00:00:56.020
Trees that had never cast a shadow on anything.

00:00:57.770 --> 00:01:00.575
This is the story of what happened next.

00:01:00.575 --> 00:01:01.837
It took four days.

00:01:01.837 --> 00:01:03.520
Tony would say it shows.

00:01:16.570 --> 00:01:19.086
Thursday, the fifteenth of October.

00:01:19.086 --> 00:01:21.890
Twenty-nine minutes past ten, at night.

00:01:23.140 --> 00:01:28.272
While the rest of the world was asleep, one commit landed.

00:01:28.272 --> 00:01:28.891
Ingest.

00:01:28.891 --> 00:01:29.599
Library.

00:01:29.599 --> 00:01:30.661
Retargeting.

00:01:30.661 --> 00:01:31.280
Studio.

00:01:32.530 --> 00:01:35.166
Eight minutes later: view standards.

00:01:35.166 --> 00:01:38.900
Projections, direction sets, mirroring, scale lock.

00:01:40.150 --> 00:01:44.723
Fifteen minutes after that: export formats for every engine that mattered.

00:01:44.723 --> 00:01:47.257
Most companies would call that a quarter.

00:01:47.257 --> 00:01:48.740
We called it a Thursday.

00:01:49.990 --> 00:01:52.400
Twenty-six Synty packs went in.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.043
Nine thousand three hundred props.

00:01:55.043 --> 00:01:57.841
One thousand and ninety-one weapons.

00:01:57.841 --> 00:02:00.717
Four hundred and fourteen characters.

00:02:00.717 --> 00:02:03.360
One hundred and thirteen vehicles.

00:02:04.610 --> 00:02:09.200
And three thousand and fifty-nine animations, waiting for a body to live in.

00:02:15.350 --> 00:02:18.568
Here is the problem every game developer knows.

00:02:18.568 --> 00:02:20.348
You have beautiful 3D art.

00:02:20.348 --> 00:02:21.717
You need 2D sprites.

00:02:21.717 --> 00:02:23.223
And between the two...

00:02:23.223 --> 00:02:24.250
lies suffering.

00:02:25.500 --> 00:02:28.040
The Synty Sprite Generator ends the suffering.

00:02:29.590 --> 00:02:30.675
You pick a model.

00:02:30.675 --> 00:02:31.888
You pick its moves.

00:02:31.888 --> 00:02:40.380
It retargets any animation onto any skeleton, puts the right weapon in the right hand, and renders every frame, from every direction.

00:02:41.630 --> 00:02:42.881
Eight directions.

00:02:42.881 --> 00:02:43.617
Isometric.

00:02:43.617 --> 00:02:51.195
Real scale, locked to the tile, so a soldier is the size of a soldier and a tank is the size of a tank.

00:02:51.195 --> 00:02:52.666
That sounds obvious.

00:02:52.666 --> 00:02:53.770
Nobody does it.

00:02:55.020 --> 00:02:57.651
It knows where the muzzle is on every frame.

00:02:57.651 --> 00:02:58.728
Where the hand is.

00:02:58.728 --> 00:03:00.881
When the grenade leaves the fingers.

00:03:00.881 --> 00:03:04.290
It writes it all down, so the game doesn't have to guess.

00:03:05.540 --> 00:03:07.216
Objects have states.

00:03:07.216 --> 00:03:08.807
A bunker is intact.

00:03:08.807 --> 00:03:10.399
Then it is damaged.

00:03:10.399 --> 00:03:13.750
Then it is a smoking hole in the ground.

00:03:13.750 --> 00:03:14.672
One sprite.

00:03:14.672 --> 00:03:15.677
Every state.

00:03:15.677 --> 00:03:17.520
Every collision shape.

00:03:23.670 --> 00:03:25.368
But sprites are not enough.

00:03:25.368 --> 00:03:27.570
A soldier needs somewhere to stand.

00:03:28.820 --> 00:03:32.320
So the engine learned to paint the ground.

00:03:32.320 --> 00:03:32.820
Grass.

00:03:32.820 --> 00:03:33.237
Sand.

00:03:33.237 --> 00:03:33.653
Snow.

00:03:33.653 --> 00:03:33.987
Mud.

00:03:33.987 --> 00:03:34.487
Water.

00:03:34.487 --> 00:03:39.820
Every tile a perfect diamond, every edge blending into the next.

00:03:41.070 --> 00:03:43.530
Then it learned to build maps.

00:03:43.530 --> 00:03:44.843
Roads that wind.

00:03:44.843 --> 00:03:46.319
Rivers with fords.

00:03:46.319 --> 00:03:48.451
Forests scattered by rule.

00:03:48.451 --> 00:03:52.470
Bunkers, fences, minefields, placed by the metre.

00:03:53.720 --> 00:03:56.827
And here is the part that changes everything.

00:03:56.827 --> 00:04:01.591
All of it, every tile, every tree, every tank, can be built by an AI.

00:04:01.591 --> 00:04:03.317
Through the command line.

00:04:03.317 --> 00:04:04.145
Through MCP.

00:04:04.145 --> 00:04:07.321
It describes the world, and the world appears.

00:04:07.321 --> 00:04:11.740
Then it looks at a picture of what it made, and makes it better.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:21.229
A tool is only as good as the thing it builds.

00:04:21.229 --> 00:04:23.140
So we did something radical.

00:04:24.390 --> 00:04:25.831
We built a game.

00:04:25.831 --> 00:04:26.822
A real one.

00:04:26.822 --> 00:04:28.264
Solitary Strike.

00:04:28.264 --> 00:04:31.146
One soldier, behind enemy lines.

00:04:32.396 --> 00:04:34.923
And we gave the game one rule.

00:04:34.923 --> 00:04:37.365
You may not touch the engine.

00:04:37.365 --> 00:04:39.049
You may only ask it.

00:04:39.049 --> 00:04:40.144
Command line.

00:04:40.144 --> 00:04:40.481
MCP.

00:04:40.481 --> 00:04:41.576
Nothing else.

00:04:42.826 --> 00:04:48.608
Every time the game needed something the engine couldn't do, it wrote it down.

00:04:48.608 --> 00:04:49.868
A feedback entry.

00:04:49.868 --> 00:04:50.535
Numbered.

00:04:50.535 --> 00:04:50.980
Dated.

00:04:50.980 --> 00:04:52.166
Brutally honest.

00:04:53.416 --> 00:04:55.026
Ninety-nine of them.

00:04:55.026 --> 00:04:57.118
The engine read every one.

00:04:57.118 --> 00:04:58.245
It fixed them.

00:04:58.245 --> 00:05:03.316
The game came back, deleted its workaround, and wrote one word.

00:05:03.316 --> 00:05:04.040
Verified.

00:05:04.040 --> 00:05:06.616
Sixty-seven times, and counting.

00:05:08.766 --> 00:05:12.942
Some of those bugs were found by over a thousand automated tests.

00:05:12.942 --> 00:05:18.146
Some were found by agents, working all night, in ten parallel copies of the code.

00:05:19.396 --> 00:05:21.491
And some were found by Tony.

00:05:21.491 --> 00:05:22.688
Tony has a gift.

00:05:22.688 --> 00:05:29.346
He looks at the thing everyone else has stared at for six hours, and he says the obvious.

00:05:29.346 --> 00:05:30.020
Out loud.

00:05:30.020 --> 00:05:30.843
Every time.

00:05:30.843 --> 00:05:32.264
He is always right.

00:05:32.264 --> 00:05:33.536
It is unbearable.

00:05:39.886 --> 00:05:42.125
How do you build this much, this fast?

00:05:42.125 --> 00:05:44.246
You don't do it one thing at a time.

00:05:45.496 --> 00:05:46.800
You do it in waves.

00:05:46.800 --> 00:05:50.437
Ten agents at once, each in its own copy of the code.

00:05:50.437 --> 00:05:53.387
One teaches soldiers to put their hands up.

00:05:53.387 --> 00:05:56.201
One splits a tank's turret from its hull.

00:05:56.201 --> 00:05:58.053
One lays fences end to end.

00:05:58.053 --> 00:06:01.896
One makes the search engine understand the word hostage.

00:06:03.146 --> 00:06:04.344
Each one tested.

00:06:04.344 --> 00:06:05.543
Each one merged.

00:06:05.543 --> 00:06:10.036
Over a thousand automated tests, passing, every single wave.

00:06:11.286 --> 00:06:12.199
Twelve waves.

00:06:12.199 --> 00:06:14.868
Three hundred and thirty-four commits.

00:06:14.868 --> 00:06:17.327
Eighty-five thousand lines of code.

00:06:17.327 --> 00:06:18.240
In four days.

00:06:18.240 --> 00:06:22.876
Andrew estimates it is only a few million commits away from ready.

00:06:29.226 --> 00:06:29.760
And this...

00:06:29.760 --> 00:06:30.586
is what it built.

00:06:31.936 --> 00:06:32.747
One commando.

00:06:32.747 --> 00:06:39.109
Dropped behind enemy lines, with three supply pods and a clock that does not care about your feelings.

00:06:40.359 --> 00:06:41.549
Twelve missions.

00:06:41.549 --> 00:06:42.888
Temperate forests.

00:06:42.888 --> 00:06:43.408
Desert.

00:06:43.408 --> 00:06:43.929
Arctic.

00:06:43.929 --> 00:06:45.044
Jungle at dusk.

00:06:45.044 --> 00:06:52.779
Each map a hundred and twenty-eight by two hundred and fifty-six metres, every metre made by the engine.

00:06:54.029 --> 00:06:55.583
Machine-gun nests.

00:06:55.583 --> 00:06:57.138
Hidden minefields.

00:06:57.138 --> 00:06:57.915
Trenches.

00:06:57.915 --> 00:07:02.319
Tanks, that only a rocket or a time bomb will stop.

00:07:03.569 --> 00:07:04.700
Blow the depot.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:06.209
Steal the code book.

00:07:06.209 --> 00:07:11.037
Capture the officer, and he surrenders, and he follows you home.

00:07:11.037 --> 00:07:12.470
Free the prisoners.

00:07:12.470 --> 00:07:14.959
Photograph the prototype, unseen.

00:07:16.209 --> 00:07:17.709
Then call the plane.

00:07:17.709 --> 00:07:18.609
And hold on.

00:07:20.759 --> 00:07:22.862
It runs in your browser.

00:07:22.862 --> 00:07:24.089
On your phone.

00:07:24.089 --> 00:07:25.404
On your tablet.

00:07:25.404 --> 00:07:26.280
Right now.

00:07:26.280 --> 00:07:27.069
For free.

00:07:29.619 --> 00:07:33.516
Today, Solitary Strike is played all over the world.

00:07:33.516 --> 00:07:34.115
By Tony.

00:07:41.265 --> 00:07:43.591
Monday, the nineteenth of October.

00:07:43.591 --> 00:07:45.096
Seventeen forty-seven.

00:07:45.096 --> 00:07:47.695
The first playtester enters the field.

00:07:49.045 --> 00:07:50.414
His first finding.

00:07:50.414 --> 00:07:52.847
An enemy soldier, incapacitated.

00:07:52.847 --> 00:07:56.345
In his words, overwhelmed by holding that gun.

00:07:56.345 --> 00:07:58.855
And somehow, impossible to shoot.

00:08:00.405 --> 00:08:03.130
Undeterred, he destroys a tank.

00:08:03.130 --> 00:08:04.713
With a LAW rocket.

00:08:04.713 --> 00:08:06.471
Exactly as designed.

00:08:06.471 --> 00:08:08.845
History will remember this.

00:08:10.595 --> 00:08:12.071
He clears the stage.

00:08:12.071 --> 00:08:14.358
He reaches the extraction zone.

00:08:14.358 --> 00:08:16.055
He waits for the plane.

00:08:18.005 --> 00:08:18.804
And he waits.

00:08:18.804 --> 00:08:24.395
Standing, and I quote, with his dick in his hand, waiting for a plane that is never coming.

00:08:27.345 --> 00:08:28.606
There was a key.

00:08:28.606 --> 00:08:28.763
C.

00:08:28.763 --> 00:08:29.945
Call the plane.

00:08:29.945 --> 00:08:32.152
It had been there all along.

00:08:32.152 --> 00:08:34.358
He found it in a screenshot.

00:08:34.358 --> 00:08:35.225
Afterwards.

00:08:36.975 --> 00:08:39.407
His final report was two words long.

00:08:39.407 --> 00:08:40.015
The fuck.

00:08:43.165 --> 00:08:49.131
Less than three hours later, wave twelve put it on the screen, in plain English.

00:08:49.131 --> 00:08:49.653
Then C.

00:08:49.653 --> 00:08:50.771
Call the plane.

00:08:50.771 --> 00:08:51.964
Thank you, Tony.

00:08:51.964 --> 00:08:54.425
Head of Pointing Out the Obvious.

00:09:00.975 --> 00:09:03.150
You may have seen the first film.

00:09:03.150 --> 00:09:03.941
Sidefighter.

00:09:03.941 --> 00:09:09.675
Two mercenaries, a fireball, and a man named Ryker, who did not become a better person.

00:09:10.925 --> 00:09:17.814
Since it premiered, earlier tonight, the engine has taught Ryker to dash forwards, by playing his dash backwards.

00:09:17.814 --> 00:09:20.191
It found the foot that did the kicking.

00:09:20.191 --> 00:09:22.325
It made his fireball spin in place.

00:09:23.575 --> 00:09:26.421
Ryker is still not a better person.

00:09:26.421 --> 00:09:27.397
Same engine.

00:09:27.397 --> 00:09:28.211
Same rule.

00:09:28.211 --> 00:09:30.325
Completely different game.

00:09:32.675 --> 00:09:34.665
Four days ago, there was nothing.

00:09:37.015 --> 00:09:42.909
Today there are twelve thousand models that can walk, run, fight, burn and fall.

00:09:42.909 --> 00:09:44.972
A hundred and fifty sprites.

00:09:44.972 --> 00:09:46.077
Seventeen maps.

00:09:46.077 --> 00:09:46.814
Two games.

00:09:46.814 --> 00:09:51.235
And one engine that makes the next one easier than the last.

00:09:53.185 --> 00:09:53.439
Oh.

00:09:53.439 --> 00:09:55.045
And one more thing.

00:09:57.595 --> 00:09:58.260
This film.

00:09:58.260 --> 00:10:00.321
The shots, the music, the edit.

00:10:00.321 --> 00:10:02.715
The voice you are hearing right now.

00:10:02.715 --> 00:10:06.705
Made on the same machine, by the same process, this evening.

00:10:08.455 --> 00:10:10.534
We didn't just build a sprite engine.

00:10:10.534 --> 00:10:12.895
We built the thing that builds the things.

00:10:14.845 --> 00:10:15.909
From nothing.

00:10:15.909 --> 00:10:17.055
To everything.

00:10:18.605 --> 00:10:19.074
Tony.

00:10:19.074 --> 00:10:21.418
If you are watching this.

00:10:21.418 --> 00:10:23.575
It's not janky anymore.

00:10:23.575 --> 00:10:24.325
Press C.
